WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.220
Thor: Love and Thunder will see Natalie Portman's
Jane Foster taking up the mantle of the Mighty

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.080
Thor, so where does that leave Chris Hemsworth's
Thor?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.380
Here's everything we know, and everything
Marvel fans can expect when the movie arrives

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.380
in theaters.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.720
Unless you've been living under a rock, you
probably know that the Thor in Avengers: Endgame

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.840
looks a bit different from the chiseled God
of Thunder we've seen in the last decade.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:27.660
Sporting a luscious gut where his six-pack
once was, the latest version of Asgard's former

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.500
king was met with mixed reception.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.100
So what does that mean for Thor: Love and
Thunder?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.560
On one hand, it does make sense to take the
fans' criticism into consideration.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.660
That being said, how exactly do you explain
Thor losing his dad bod while he's in space?

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.670
Unless Taika Waititi can come up with a feasible
explanation for how Thor slimmed down in the

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.690
time that's passed since the events of Endgame,
don't be surprised to see another round of

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.600
Bro Thor on the horizon.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.720
Speaking of the Guardians, what kind of role
will they play in Thor: Love and Thunder?

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.020
Although Kevin Feige did confirm that there
will be a Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 at

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.380
some point in the future, it's clear that
Thor's fourth solo outing will precede it.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.860
Considering that Thor was last seen on board
the Benatar with the Guardians, is it safe

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.220
to assume that they'll also make an appearance
in Thor: Love and Thunder?

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.280
If they do, will there be enough screen time
to go around?

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.680
Don't forget that in addition to Jane Foster
becoming the Mighty Thor, the film will also

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.520
include Tessa Thompson's Valkyrie finding
a queen.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.080
Thor's new space besties may need to take
a breather for the time being.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.240
You know that awkward feeling when you see
an ex out in public?

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.180
Imagine how much worse it would be if that
ex was stealing your superpower.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:41.520
In Ragnarok, Thor unconvincingly claims that
he was the one who dumped Jane when questioned

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.539
by some fans.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.020
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.140
"She didn't dump me, I dumped her.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.240
It was a mutual dumping."

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:54.840
Later, one of the MCU's go-to writers, Christopher
Markus, confirmed that Endgame almost featured

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.520
a reunion scene with Thor and Jane.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.300
What's the deal with these star-crossed lovers?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.800
It's worth noting that Thor's most successful
solo movie was the only one without Jane in

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.300
it.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.780
Is it safe to assume that Waititi is going
to try a fresh new angle with the characters,

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.100
since clearly their romance wasn't translating
onscreen the way Marvel thought it would?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.560
If so, don't expect much in the way of a rekindling
between these former flames, Thor: Love and

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.280
Thunder could instead find Chris Hemsworth
and Natalie Portman as friends and allies

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.500
rather than lovers.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.480
"Oh, you know, Jane and I aren't even dating
anymore, so.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.240
These things happen, though.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.320
You know, nothing lasts forever.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.080
The only thing that--"

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:32.580
"Why don't you come sit down-"

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.160
"I'm not done, yet, dude."

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:39.080
In a 2014 comic book event Original Sin, Thor
lost the ability to lift Mjolnir.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.300
The trusty hammer was eventually picked up
by a cancer-ridden Jane Foster, granting her

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.100
the powers and mantle of Thor.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.180
While the twist played out well on the comics
page, earlier Thor films have already played

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.560
withThor losing Mjolnir.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.360
Hela reduces Mjolnir to pieces in Ragnarok,
and Odin even deemed Thor unworthy of his

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.680
hammer way back in the first Thor film.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.080
Would Waititi yet again go down this seemingly
well-worn path?

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.180
If Thor: Love and Thunder includes yet another
instance where Thor's worthiness is brought

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.840
into question, there's a good chance fans
might perceive that as lazy writing.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:14.150
The fraternal relationship between Thor and
Loki has been one of the best-developed arcs

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.140
in the MCU.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.620
Tom Hiddleston's Loki evolved from enemy to
ally over the course of the three previous

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.120
Thor movies, and his early death at the hands
of Thanos in Avengers: Infinity War was a

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.580
sad moment for fans.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.170
Although the time-traveling in Endgame opened
the door for more Loki in the future, it sounds

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.340
like he'll be limited to a series on Disney+,
and won't be interacting with the current

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.480
MCU timeline.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.940
How will his brother's seemingly permanent
death affect the character?

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:44.020
Infinity War and Endgame explored the heavy
toll that excessive loss took on Thor's psyche,

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.600
and Loki is at the root of that.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.460
Has Chris Hemsworth's Thor fully come to grips
with losing someone like Loki, or is a part

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.480
of him still in mourning?

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.800
Will Thor: Love and Thunder mark Chris Hemsworth's
final appearance in the MCU?

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:01.320
With Natalie Portman's Jane Foster taking
up the mantle, now could be an appropriate

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.250
time for Hemsworth to also pass the torch.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.220
However, don't count your hammers before they
arrive.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.220
"What am I looking at?"

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.860
"Sometimes it takes a second."

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.879
When speaking with Variety in May of 2019,
Hemsworth admitted that he wasn't ready to

00:04:19.879 --> 00:04:21.480
hang up the hammer quite yet:

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.440
"I'd still love to do more, to be honest…I
feel like we've opened up such a different

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:25.940
character.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.000
I feel more energized for the possibility
of where it could go."

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.219
Whether, Love and Thunder is Hemsworth's last
swing at the character or just another step

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:37.500
on Thor's journey, we'll just have to wait
for November 5, 2021 to find out.

